---
import Layout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy and Billing Policy">
  <section class="py-16">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8 dark:text-white">Sotomayor Consulting Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">Effective date: 04-12-2023. Last updated: 09-21-2026.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-gray-300 bg-gray-50 p-5 text-gray-800 dark:border-gray-600 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:text-white" aria-labelledby="independence-notice">
        <h2 id="independence-notice" class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Important notice: we are a private, independent company</h2>
        <p>
          Sotomayor Consulting International is not a government entity and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or authorized to represent the United States Government or any other public agency. We provide private professional guidance, document preparation, and administrative support; we do not issue official documents or decide government applications.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Approvals, denials, processing times, and the issuance of registrations, identification numbers, permits, or visas are determined exclusively by the appropriate government authority. Our professional fees are separate from applicable government fees, as specified in the scope of services provided to the client. When the procedure allows it, you may submit your application directly to the official agency without hiring our services.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          At Sotomayor Consulting (hereinafter, "we", "us" or "our"), we are committed to protecting and respecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, store, share, and protect personal information you provide when you use our website sotomayorconsulting.com and our services.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">2. Information We Collect</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We collect personal information that you provide directly to us, as well as information we obtain from your use of our services. Personal information is any information that can identify you or be linked to you, such as your name, email address, phone number, postal address, and tax identification number.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">3. How We Use the Information Collected</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We use the personal information we collect to provide private guidance and support for the formation and maintenance of legal entities, prepare or facilitate documents for submission to third parties or appropriate authorities, improve and personalize your experience, communicate with you, comply with our legal obligations, and for general business purposes. Our processing of this information does not make Sotomayor Consulting International a public authority and does not mean that we issue or approve government registrations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">4. How We Share the Information Collected</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We do not sell or rent your personal information to third parties. We only share your personal information with third parties as described in this Privacy Policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">5. How We Store and Protect the Information Collected</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We store your personal information securely and take measures to protect it against loss, misuse, unauthorized access, disclosure, alteration, and destruction. However, no security measure is infallible, so we cannot guarantee the absolute security of your personal information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We retain your personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes for which it was collected, unless the law requires or permits a longer retention period.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">7. International Data Transfer</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          In some cases, we may transfer personal information we collect from you to other countries different from your country of residence. By providing us with personal information, you consent to such transfer, storage, and processing. We ensure that appropriate measures are taken to protect your personal information in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">8. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          In accordance with applicable laws, you have certain rights regarding the personal information we collect about you. These rights may include the right to access, correct, update, delete, or restrict the use of your personal information. If you wish to exercise any of these rights, please contact us through the contact information provided at the end of this Privacy Policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">9. Changes to Our Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          We may occasionally update our Privacy Policy. If we make changes to this Privacy Policy, we will notify you by posting the updated Privacy Policy on our website and updating the effective date at the top of this Privacy Policy. We recommend that you review this Privacy Policy periodically to stay informed about how we protect your personal information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mt-16 mb-8 dark:text-white">ANNUAL BILLING POLICY</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">Last updated: August 2025</p>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">1. Applicable to LLC (Limited Liability Company)</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 dark:text-white">Clients incorporated during the year 2025</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          In January 2026, it will be necessary to renew the Registered Agent service and pay the corresponding state fee (the value varies by State).
          The Registered Agent charge for the first year will be proportional to the date of incorporation.
          Example: If XYZ LLC is incorporated on March 15, 2025, in January 2026 you will be billed only for the months elapsed until that date:
          March 2025 – January 2026 = 10 months
          Calculation: 399 × (10/12) = 332.50
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white mt-4">
          From the second year onward, the annual maintenance charge will be the full current value.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 mt-4 dark:text-white">Notifications and payment deadlines</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          Clients will receive an email at the beginning of the year with details of the amount and due date for annual maintenance.
          Additionally, a weekly reminder will be sent while there is a pending payment balance.
          If payment has not been made by February 15, a late processing fee of 300 USD may be applied.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">2. Applicable to LP (Limited Partnership)</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 dark:text-white">Incorporated clients</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          Clients will receive an email notification two (2) months before the company's incorporation anniversary date, informing the amount and due date for annual maintenance.

          Example: If ABC LP is incorporated on June 20, 2025, you will receive the first notification on April 20, 2026.
          A weekly email notification will be sent regarding the maintenance payment.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2 mt-4 dark:text-white">Deadlines and late payment fees</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          If payment has not been made by two (2) weeks before the company's anniversary date, a late processing fee of 300 USD may be applied.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-8 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">3. General Considerations</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          All amounts mentioned are expressed in USD.
          Deadlines and fees may be subject to changes in accordance with current legislation or adjustments to State Services (State Fee) and Registered Agent rates.
          It is the client's responsibility to keep their contact information up to date to receive notifications in a timely manner.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 dark:text-white">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4 dark:text-white">How to Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white">
          If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy or the handling of your personal information by Sotomayor Consulting, please contact us through the following contact information:
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-white mt-4">
          <strong>Sotomayor Consulting</strong><br>
          Quito, Ecuador<br>
          Email: info@sotomayorconsulting.com<br>
          Phone: +593 98 324 5863
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
